{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1521897-coils-of-the-dragon-to-vtm","id":1521897,"title":"Coils of the Dragon to VtM?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-09-02T11:12:16-07:00","id":1521897,"title":"Coils of the Dragon to VtM?","content":"This is something which I have thought about as it adress two points for me.<br /> <br /> The first one is to bring cool Requiem stuff over to Masquerade, and Coils of the Dragon are among them.<br /> <br /> The second is that the Road/Path of Metamorphsis seems to me that it is, in standard VtM lore, a lifestyle for deluded idiots. They've been at transendence and that for thousands of years and have exactly nothing to show for all their time and energy.<br /> <br /> Thus a loose idea I have is to tie access to buy Coils of the Dragon to adhering to said Road/Path. Hopefully that could make players see a reason to follow these teachings and make the followers of this Road/Path seem scary as they might be on to something as opposed to just flailing about and being stupid.<br /> <br /> What do you guys think about this idea of allowing the Road/Path of Metamorphsis allow the buying of Coils of the Dragon? Or would it just be a different version of a Clan tied so closely to a special Discipline that the Clan is reglated to second place in regards to the Discipline?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","name":"Gurkhal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"863"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-02T13:55:11-07:00","id":1521901,"title":"","content":"I feel Coils of the Dragon requires a completely new path of enlightenment. One that leans less towards body horror, and more towards a subtle transcendence. In regards to clan, since Coils of the Dragon tend to be very scholarly pursuit which pushes one to go beyond their limits, I think clan will be regarded as secondary and only seen as a factor that could have some effect on how quickly and easily you learn coils, as well as which ones you prefer, similar to how it was in VTR.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/pub/18.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27313-hello","name":"Hello","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27313_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-02T15:11:37-07:00","id":1521920,"title":"","content":"The closest that the Path of Metamorphosis comes to <i>requiring</i> body horror is in relation to its emphasis on general experimentation and altering one's own flesh, both of which can veer pretty far from tentacle orgies and living furniture in practice. Honestly, the bigger obstacle to tying the Coils to this Path is that asking and answering questions constitute sins against it at higher levels, while the Coils themselves suggest a level of standardization and codification of knowledge/technique that seems unlikely if everyone's working toward their own answers and jealously hoarding every scrap of insight they pick up along the way. The Path of Bones/Death and Soul and the Path of Scorched Heart actually seem more conducive to their development since they're better at collaboration, and thus better poised to support or debunk claims through replication; the scholarly bent of the Path of Caine and its interest in challenging the limits of the vampiric condition also seems like a good fit for the Coils, though I can also see them being hostile to them as attempts to reject and abandon one's vampiric nature.<br /> <br /> The Metamorphosists obviously have a very avid interest in transcending vampiric weaknesses, but the path taken would probably be considerably more anomalous and personal; if anything, I'd make them exhibit a capacity to blur the lines between Coils in strange ways rather than have them establish a monopoly over the Coils themselves. Maybe they, or at least some of them, would be more like caitiffs in relation to the Coils: lacking a specialty and thus a Coil that they have a particular affinity to, but having more free-form access to them through independent research.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27894-paramecius","name":"Paramecius","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27894_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-03T04:06:43-07:00","id":1521968,"title":"","content":"It is a bit strange how the Path of Metamorphosis ended up as the &quot;reason&quot; of body horror<br /> Tho' understandable... in a sense<br /> In South Slavic folklore, a vampire was believed to pass through several distinct stages in its development. The first 40 days were considered decisive for the making of a vampire; it started out as an invisible shadow and then gradually gained strength from the lifeblood of the living, forming a (typically invisible) jelly-like, boneless mass, and eventually building up a human-like body nearly identical to the one the person had had in life. This development allowed the creature to ultimately leave its grave and begin a new life as a human. The vampire, who was usually male, was also sexually active and could have children, either with his widow or a new wife. These could become vampires themselves, but could also have a special ability to see and kill vampires, allowing them to become vampire hunters.<br /> The bodies of <i>vrykolakas</i> have the same distinctive characteristics as the bodies of vampires in Balkan folklore. They do not decay; instead, they swell and may even attain a &quot;drumlike&quot; form, being very large, have a ruddy complexion, and are, according to one account, &quot;fresh and gorged with new blood&quot;.\u200b in Greek folklore, the <i>vrykolakas</i> are described more as cannibals than bloodsuckers with a taste in particular for human livers\u200b<br /> This a bit obsucre slavic folklore was - I think - where the Tzimisce and their power came from<br /> And of course, the &quot;changing body&quot; is somewhat the base of every vampiric myth; - the natural characteristics of decomposition\u2014such as receding gums and the appearance of growing hair and fingernails\u2014reinforced the belief that corpses were in fact continuing some manner of life after death and transform<br /> <br /> But the Path of Metamorphosis only considers a &quot;sin&quot; to neglect to alter one's own body with the reason, physical change must be attained before any more significant metamorphosis - and NOT requires anywhere to be the Thing from John Carpenter's movie<br /> The Path study the Beast's limits and the limits of vampirism in general and the main tenent is the world is made up of evolutionary chains. Animals are below humans, who are below the Kindred.<br /> Logically, the next step is defining and attaining the state of being beyond the curse of vampirism- next step is a state akin to apotheosis, the state of Azhi Dahaka, an enlightened and ultimate state of being,<br /> And mainly thanks to the powers of Vicissitude the followers believe they have the potential to transcend the constraints of the flesh.\u200b\u200b<br /> The general consensus regarding Azhi Dahaka seems to be that it is a state of inverted nirv\u0101\u1e47a, where the Tzimisce becomes a truly self-sufficient will within the universe, divorced from Creation and beholden to nothing.<br /> The alterations is not becasue of the &quot;need&quot; of body horror or tentacle orgies, but because of the realisation of the potential in the undead form - strengthen thebones to weather crushing blows or sharpen them into pikes for impaling enemies, relaocate organs to make their digestion of blood more efficient (tho' this one was always a bit strange since vampiric organs are useless and they are more like sponges, storing vitae in their body, not in liver, nor have a circulation... ) and many Metamorphosists feed only on their fellow Cainites, believing that an aversion to mortal blood is a sign of metaphysical superiority<br /> Since aquiring a Phrygian Codex or indeed a Tutor who will guide you in the path is rare (in fact asking another for knowledge is a &quot;sin&quot; with the reason lessons of Metamorphosis are secrets that must be uncovered, not copied and Sharing knowledge with another is also a &quot;sin&quot;, with the reason Knowledge must be learned, not simply illustrated) every traveller of this lonely road reach their destination alone and any result or idea comes only from inside, so to speak; members becasue of this reason are mostly cold, inhuman and exactingly scientific... but it is not a requirment! Transformation into something else could mean anything.<br /> Some are altering their flesh in various means until they no longer have a recognizable gender or look even remotely human and of course experiment on others, but at the end of the day, body horror or tentacles, or anything the Tzimsice infamous for... are not a requirment<br /> Actually from a Metamorphosist point of view - tho' there are no two similar traveller - such thing are probably useless.<br /> Eons ago, and from all it begun, distraught over its tethered existence, the Eldest spent a mortal\u2019s age in seclusion and meditation, shifting and flying through shapes of mortal and legend alike, seeking out a form free of the accursed thirst. It studied the scrolls that once gifted it with spellcraft, hoping to find answers within its fading mortal gifts. It mattered little, however, for the thirst came of the Beast, and it drowned all considerations. The Eldest could not escape, for while it changed forms, it could not change its essence. Cruel fate deprived it of that one saving grace mortals possessed: adaptation as a tool of survival.<br /> From this basic realisation bloomed the Path of Metamorphosis and it took ten+ millenia to the Eldest to achieve it, but not with body horror, but shapeshiting to experience the forms and their capabilites<br /> Vicissitude and Protean to alter the self, Animalsim to possess Animals and Dominate to posessess Humans to experience the world from their body, Auspex to have a Sight beyond Sight are the bread and butter of a Metamorphosis, not tentacles, gore and vore and living furnitures<br /> At least in my humble opinion<br /> So the Coils of the Dragon in V:tM is very wel in the lines of Metamorphosis","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23890,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","user":"Shadeprowler","date":". 09-03-2023, 07:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-03T04:11:43-07:00