nsus regarding Azhi Dahaka seems to be that it is a state of inverted nirv\u0101\u1e47a, where the Tzimisce becomes a truly self-sufficient will within the universe, divorced from Creation and beholden to nothing.<br /> The alterations is not becasue of the &quot;need&quot; of body horror or tentacle orgies, but because of the realisation of the potential in the undead form - strengthen thebones to weather crushing blows or sharpen them into pikes for impaling enemies, relaocate organs to make their digestion of blood more efficient (tho' this one was always a bit strange since vampiric organs are useless and they are more like sponges, storing vitae in their body, not in liver, nor have a circulation... ) and many Metamorphosists feed only on their fellow Cainites, believing that an aversion to mortal blood is a sign of metaphysical superiority<br /> Since aquiring a Phrygian Codex or indeed a Tutor who will guide you in the path is rare (in fact asking another for knowledge is a &quot;sin&quot; with the reason lessons of Metamorphosis are secrets that must be uncovered, not copied and Sharing knowledge with another is also a &quot;sin&quot;, with the reason Knowledge must be learned, not simply illustrated) every traveller of this lonely road reach their destination alone and any result or idea comes only from inside, so to speak; members becasue of this reason are mostly cold, inhuman and exactingly scientific... but it is not a requirment! Transformation into something else could mean anything.<br /> Some are altering their flesh in various means until they no longer have a recognizable gender or look even remotely human and of course experiment on others, but at the end of the day, body horror or tentacles, or anything the Tzimsice infamous for... are not a requirment<br /> Actually from a Metamorphosist point of view - tho' there are no two similar traveller - such thing are probably useless.<br /> Eons ago, and from all it begun, distraught over its tethered existence, the Eldest spent a mortal\u2019s age in seclusion and meditation, shifting and flying through shapes of mortal and legend alike, seeking out a form free of the accursed thirst. It studied the scrolls that once gifted it with spellcraft, hoping to find answers within its fading mortal gifts. It mattered little, however, for the thirst came of the Beast, and it drowned all considerations. The Eldest could not escape, for while it changed forms, it could not change its essence. Cruel fate deprived it of that one saving grace mortals possessed: adaptation as a tool of survival.<br /> From this basic realisation bloomed the Path of Metamorphosis and it took ten+ millenia to the Eldest to achieve it, but not with body horror, but shapeshiting to experience the forms and their capabilites<br /> Vicissitude and Protean to alter the self, Animalsim to possess Animals and Dominate to posessess Humans to experience the world from their body, Auspex to have a Sight beyond Sight are the bread and butter of a Metamorphosis, not tentacles, gore and vore and living furnitures<br /> At least in my humble opinion<br /> So the Coils of the Dragon in V:tM is very wel in the lines of Metamorphosis</div> </div> </div> </div>Requiem has - kind of - those original body horror vampires with the Pijavica. It's actually a rather limited/limiting Clan but it exists and it's really a unisue kind of Vampire there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1233-ur-than","name":"Ur-Than","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1233_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"253"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-06T01:56:34-07:00","id":1522144,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hello</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1521897-coils-of-the-dragon-to-vtm?p=1521901#post1521901\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel Coils of the Dragon requires a completely new path of enlightenment. One that leans less towards body horror, and more towards a subtle transcendence. In regards to clan, since Coils of the Dragon tend to be very scholarly pursuit which pushes one to go beyond their limits, I think clan will be regarded as secondary and only seen as a factor that could have some effect on how quickly and easily you learn coils, as well as which ones you prefer, similar to how it was in VTR.</div> </div> </div> </div></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">While one could do a new Road, or a Path within the Road of Metamorphosis I would hope to not have to do extra work in writing up a new Path or an entirely new Road to make the Coils accessible.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">As for Clan I was more thinking about the phenomena that players pick a Clan due to access to a special Discipline and then the themes and concepts of the Clan don\u2019t matter for the character as the player just wanted a cool/powerful Discipline at a cheaper cost. That\u2019s what I meant with Clan being secondary.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">In regards to this scenario I would think one could see it as a character that does the absolutely minimum required to keep a Road, get the Coils and then do something entirely different from what the Road is supposed to be about, which is what the player wanted to do from the start, but with access to the Coils.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Paramecius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1521897-coils-of-the-dragon-to-vtm?p=1521920#post1521920\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The closest that the Path of Metamorphosis comes to <i>requiring</i> body horror is in relation to its emphasis on general experimentation and altering one's own flesh, both of which can veer pretty far from tentacle orgies and living furniture in practice. Honestly, the bigger obstacle to tying the Coils to this Path is that asking and answering questions constitute sins against it at higher levels, while the Coils themselves suggest a level of standardization and codification of knowledge/technique that seems unlikely if everyone's working toward their own answers and jealously hoarding every scrap of insight they pick up along the way.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200b</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">I agree with the body horror not required angle although body horror for shock value has become so associated with Tzimisce in general that I\u2019m not sure it\u2019s possible to divorce the two at this point.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">As for the individualistic aspect of the Road of Metamorphosis that would be a problem. Yet I am not sure of what other Roads actually exist that really strives to do what the Coils are a part of; transcending the curse of vampirism or at least its flaws. My idea with tying Coils to the Road was thus that as characters progress along the Road they would gain insight and that insight would be used to justify getting Coils to show that. Supposedly if the Road wasn\u2019t so self-centered and individualistic then its followers would probably have advanced a great deal further than what even the Coils allow.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Paramecius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1521897-coils-of-the-dragon-to-vtm?p=1521920#post1521920\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Path of Bones/Death and Soul and the Path of Scorched Heart actually seem more conducive to their development since they're better at collaboration, and thus better poised to support or debunk claims through replication; the scholarly bent of the Path of Caine and its interest in challenging the limits of the vampiric condition also seems like a good fit for the Coils, though I can also see them being hostile to them as attempts to reject and abandon one's vampiric nature.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200b</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">I totally agree that these Roads would be more suitable to cooperation and such. But what I would ask is to what degree they actually strive to transcend in a way that would explain the Coils? I don\u2019t claim to be some kind of scholar or such but when looking at them they don\u2019t make a obvious connection to seeking transcendence beyond vampirism and its nature and flaws in the way that the Road of Metamorphosis does.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Paramecius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1521897-coils-of-the-dragon-to-vtm?p=1521920#post1521920\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Metamorphosists obviously have a very avid interest in transcending vampiric weaknesses, but the path taken would probably be considerably more anomalous and personal; if anything, I'd make them exhibit a capacity to blur the lines between Coils in strange ways rather than have them establish a monopoly over the Coils themselves. Maybe they, or at least some of them, would be more like caitiffs in relation to the Coils: lacking a specialty and thus a Coil that they have a particular affinity to, but having more free-form access to them through independent research.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200b</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Making them a kind of \u201cCatiff for Coils\u201d would absolutely work but I fear it would be at the expense of making the Coils seem strange and something to seek and strive for.</span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1521897-coils-of-the-dragon-to-vtm?p=1521968#post1521968\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">It is a bit strange how the Path of Metamorphosis ended up as the &quot;reason&quot; of body horror<br /> Tho' understandable... in a sense<br /> In South Slavic folklore, a vampire was believed to pass through several distinct stages in its development. The first 40 days were considered decisive for the making of a vampire; it started out as an invisible shadow and then gradually gained strength from the lifeblood of the living, forming a (typically invisible) jelly-like, boneless mass, and eventually building up a human-like body nearly identical to the one the person had had in life. This development allowed the creature to ultimately leave its grave and begin a new life as a human. The vampire, who was usually male, was also sexually active and could have children, either with his widow or a new wife. These could become vampires themselves, but could also have a special ability to see and kill vampires, allowing them to become vampire hunters.<br /> The bodies of <i>vrykolakas</i> have the same distinctive characteristics as the bodies of vampires in Balkan folklore. They do not decay; instead, they swell and may even attain a &quot;drumlike&quot; form, being very large, have a ruddy complexion, and are, according to one account, &quot;fresh and gorged with new blood&quot;.\u200b in Greek folklore, the <i>vrykolakas</i> are described more as cannibals than bloodsuckers with a taste in particular for human livers\u200b<br /> This a bit obsucre slavic folklore was - I think - where the Tzimisce and their power came from<br /> And of course, the &quot;changing body&quot; is somewhat the base of every vampiric myth; - the natural characteristics of decomposition\u2014such as receding gums and the appearance of growing hair and fingernails\u2014reinforced the belief that corpses were in fact continuing some manner of life after death and transform</span></div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">\u200b</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">I would love for Vicissitude, Tzimisce and the Road of Metamorphosis to have a basis in mythology and folklore but I\u2019m afraid that I\u2019m entirely sold on the idea that it\u2019s not. Everything I\u2019ve seen indicates that this is &quot;merely&quot; an adaption of the Wamphyri from Brian Lumley\u2019s \u201cNecroscope\u201d series. Even if Tzimisce behaviour is not nearly as malicious, cruel and revolting as Wamphyri behaviour is.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1521897-coils-of-the-dragon-to-vtm?p=1521968#post1521968\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But the Path of Metamorphosis only considers a &quot;sin&quot; to neglect to alter one's own body with the reason, physical change must be attained before any more significant metamorphosis - and NOT requires anywhere to be the Thing from John Carpenter's movie<br /> The Path study the Beast's limits and the limits of vampirism in general and the main tenent is the world is made up of evolutionary chains. Animals are below humans, who are below the Kindred.<br /> Logically, the next step is defining and attaining the state of being beyond the curse of vampirism- next step is a state akin to apotheosis, the state of Azhi Dahaka, an enlightened and ultimate state of being,<br /> And mainly thanks to the powers of Vicissitude the followers believe they have the potential to transcend the constraints of the flesh.\u200b\u200b<br /> The general consensus regarding Azhi Dahaka seems to be that it is a state of inverted nirv\u0101\u1e47a, where the Tzimisce becomes a truly self-sufficient will within the universe, divorced from Creation and beholden to nothing.<br /> The alterations is not becasue of the &quot;need&quot; of body horror or tentacle orgies, but because of the realisation of the potential in the undead form - strengthen thebones to weather crushing blows or sharpen them into pikes for impaling enemies, relaocate organs to make their digestion of blood more efficient (tho' this one was always a bit strange since vampiric organs are useless and they are more like sponges, storing vitae in their body, not in liver, nor have a circulation... ) and many Metamorphosists feed only on their fellow Cainites, believing that an aversion to mortal blood is a sign of metaphysical superiority<br /> Since aquiring a Phrygian Codex or indeed a Tutor who will guide you in the path is rare (in fact asking another for knowledge is a &quot;sin&quot; with the reason lessons of Metamorphosis are secrets that must be uncovered, not copied and Sharing knowledge with another is also a &quot;sin&quot;, with the reason Knowledge must be learned, not simply illustrated) every traveller of this lonely road reach their destination alone and any result or idea comes only from inside, so to speak; members becasue of this reason are mostly cold, inhuman and exactingly scientific... but it is not a requirment! Transformation into something else could mean anything.<br /> Some are altering their flesh in various means until they no longer have a recognizable gender or look even remotely human and of course experiment on others, but at the end of the day, body horror or tentacles, or anything the Tzimsice infamous for... are not a requirment<br /> Actually from a Metamorphosist point of view - tho' there are no two similar traveller - such thing are probably useless.<br /> Eons ago, and from all it begun, distraught over its tethered existence, the Eldest spent a mortal\u2019s age in seclusion and meditation, shifting and flying through shapes of mortal and legend alike, seeking out a form free of the accursed thirst. It studied the scrolls that once gifted it with spellcraft, hoping to find answers within its fading mortal gifts. It mattered little, however, for the thirst came of the Beast, and it drowned all considerations. The Eldest could not escape, for while it changed forms, it could not change its essence. Cruel fate deprived it of that one saving grace mortals possessed: adaptation as a tool of survival.<br /> From this basic realisation bloomed the Path of Metamorphosis and it took ten+ millenia to the Eldest to achieve it, but not with body horror, but shapeshiting to experience the forms and their capabilites<br /> Vicissitude and Protean to alter the self, Animalsim to possess Animals and Dominate to posessess Humans to experience the world from their body, Auspex to have a Sight beyond Sight are the bread and butter of a Metamorphosis, not tentacles, gore and vore and living furnitures<br /> At least in my humble opinion<br /> So the Coils of the Dragon in V:tM is very wel in the lines of Metamorphosis</div> </div> </div> </div></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">A short reply to a long post. I pretty much agree entirely with you and thank you for the elaboration on the Road of Metamorphosis.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1521897-coils-of-the-dragon-to-vtm?p=1521969#post1521969\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Its doable, tinker with the road of metamorphosis a little but it could work. Alternatively have is as benchmarks on the path to golconda</div> </div> </div> </div></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">I could use it for Golconda but I\u2019m a bit hesistant for that, as for one reason is that my players are really not the kind of people to have their characters go look for Golconda.</span><br /> \u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","name":"Gurkhal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"863"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-06T09:01:28-07:00","id":1522160,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"970\" data-vbnamecard=\"970\">Gurkhal</a> The nest of existing quotes and codes present here makes me not want to tangle with quotes myself, so I'll simply elaborate a bit on my position without them.<br /> <br /> There's no question that in terms of ideological goals The Path of Metamorphosis would be the best fit for the Coils, but in terms of execution, I think the Coils as they exist as codified steps from A-E (or * - *****) that are the same for everyone who delves into them would be a non-starter for the Metamorphosists themselves. Other clinically and research-minded Paths are better poised to produce these sorts of results, but it is indeed true that they aren't necessarily concerned with transcending vampirism per se. That said, their values and goals do incentivize diminishing or eliminating certain <i>aspects</i> of vampirism, and that is where I see their work with the Coils coming in. For the Gravediggers/Necronomists, the study of permutations of death can extend into undeath and they are charged to achieve a state of comfort with death and unlife, which could be read as resigning oneself to a new state of existence or excising that which is burdensome from it (indeed, this could be a point of schismatic tension within the Paths); but more specifically, I imagine an interest in attaining greater distance from atavistic ties to life itself - in particular hunger and the need for blood that drives it - and thereby attaining a more &quot;pure&quot; state undeath. It's a similar situation for the Path of the Scorched Heart: they aren't a trans-vampiric movement themselves, but they'd dearly love for the Beast to shut up and sit down, and it's not hard to imagine that they'd have put in long and hard work to make it do so.<br /> <br /> Admittedly, these motivations don't necessarily map to the existing Coils in a direct way. The Unforgiving wouldn't come up with the Coil of the Wyrm (but I could see Beasts and Unifiers doing it through less clinical paradigms), for example, because even leaning into the Beast on their own terms would be considered a sign of weakness, but they might find some way to partially bind their Beasts to thralls or something and keep them on a tight leash. Similarly, a Necronomist might decide that this weakness to sunlight is BS for a walking cadaver and devise a variant of the Coil of Ascendant that develops resistance to sun and flame by becoming more corpselike (much like the Corpse in the Monster, come think of it) rather than through reliance on the blush of life.<br /> <br /> The end result of this approach is probably that there wouldn't be a singular group or Path from which all Coils arise; instead, individual Coils would be discrete achievements from individual Paths. Even so, the Path of Metamorphosis would still stand out for its more or less indiscriminate interest in Coils at a conceptual level and its adherents would often work as allies or antagonists (more often antagonists, I'd imagine) due to their drive to delve into their secrets by any means necessary. Their individualistic approach here can still bring in the strangeness of the Coils by combining them in unorthodox ways and divesting them of common assumptions.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1492891-do-any-of-you-use-the-inconnu-in-your-games-at-all?p=1521831#post1521831\">Black Fox mentioned</a> an interesting tidbit about the Inconnu that might make them a good stand-in for the Ordo Dracul without the Path of Metamorphosis' hangups if you're willing to expand the desire to eliminate the need for blood to a desire to triumph over the weaknesses of vampirism more generally; this could even be a deviant fringe within the sect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27894,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27894-paramecius","user":"Paramecius","date":". 09-06-2023, 10:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27894-paramecius","name":"Paramecius","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27894_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}